<title>BRAZIL: Brazil raises 152 mln reais with Escelsa shr sale.</title>
<headline>Brazil raises 152 mln reais with Escelsa shr sale.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil raised 152.6 million reais with the auction of common shares of privatized Espirito Santo power firm Escelsa, the Rio de Janeiro Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>A total of 782,915 voting shares was sold, of which 666,911 or 14.65 percent of Escelsa's voting capital represented federal power holding Eletrobras's remaining stake in the company, the bolsa said.</p>
<p>The stock was sold at an average price of 194.95 reais, 20.33 percent above the auction's base price, it said.</p>
<p>Garantia, Primus and Bozano, Simonsen brokerages bought the biggest lots of shares, it added.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
